+- [#93](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/93) [`a7faee0`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/a7faee013da49aa8415bad2da9f58be26e093fab) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Footage the browser can't decode now shows everywhere a film is drawn, not only in exports: `openfilm look`, posters, stills and slides, Studio's film cards, and page thumbnails. This covers ProRes, and HEVC on a computer without a chip for it. Each place draws it through the same copy an export makes. Studio's preview also plays that copy when no proxy is ready. A video exported with its subtitles burned in gets these copies too; before, its ProRes footage came out black.
+
+- [#93](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/pull/93) [`a7faee0`](https://github.com/openfilm/openfilm/commit/a7faee013da49aa8415bad2da9f58be26e093fab) Thanks [@PazChen](https://github.com/PazChen)! - Right-click a tab for its menu: rename it, show its project's folder, close it, close the other tabs or the tabs to its right. Renaming a tab now shows the selected words clearly. The chat's agent menu has a settings button at its top right that opens Settings → Agents.
